 The following directives are provided for module and class contents:
 
+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional :rst:directive:option:`canonical`
+   option describes the represented type and is shown in the signature after
+   the alias name. Its expression is parsed as a Python annotation, so
+   references to other documented objects are linked. A description may be
+   provided in the directive body, but nested object directives are not
+   allowed.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
